WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.
You look sharp.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:03.968
Thanks for being here, buddy.
-Thanks for having me, Jimmy.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:08.334
Hello, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:11.000
-You know, I was noticing a lot
of the projects

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.501
you're involved in
involve space.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.567
A lot of things like
"Prometheus" -- space --

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.968
"Doctor Strange" -- space.
-Space.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.734
-Yeah. You did "The Martian."

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:22.901
-"The Martian," yes.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.834
-Space.
-Yes. Yeah.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.100
-Are you typecast?

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.767
-Yeah, yeah, I guess I'm like
the Colin Firth of sci-fi.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:37.400
-That's exactly right, yes.
"Pride and Prejudice."

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.133
That's funny.
-I flown a fare few spaceships.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.801
So I think I've been barred now

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.234
because my insurance premium's
gone up.

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.734
-Yeah, exactly.
I have an older picture of you.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.000
Here is 1994.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.367
This is you in a stage
production of "Star Trek."

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.901
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:54.901
-Not bad.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.734
-There I am,
my little live self.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.167
What do you remember about this?

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.634
-Yeah, we had a great time
on that.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:09.167
I was playing Sulu,
and I think one of the things

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.033
what you're going to do when
you're flying spaceships,

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.601
you just sort of look off into
the middle distance

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.133
confused of where you're going.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:20.300
And there was one time they
forgot the sound effects,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.701
so I had to kind of improvise
and, you know --

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.601
[ Whistles ]
"Bridge to Captain Kirk.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.968
There appears to be some
Klingons on Uranus,"

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:33.100
or something like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.734
-You did the whistle yourself?
-The whistle, yes.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:39.400
-It's an interesting story about
how you got the role of Wong

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.000
in the first "Doctor Strange"
movie.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.434
You kind of manifested it.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:45.534
-Well, yeah. Well, as you were
saying, I was doing the film

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.501
"The Martian," with my good
friend Chiwetel Ejiofor.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.300
And you know, you're having
lunch,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.400
and "What are you up to next?"

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.267
He's doing "Doctor Strange."

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.067
You go on the Internet.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.901
There's this character called
Wong.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:01:59.868
-Hello.
-Hi. Hi!

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.334
[ Laughter ]
Hey!

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.267
-Hi! Yes.
-Yeah, my jaw drops.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.934
I didn't have an agent
at the time --

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:09.367
well, for the better part of
eight years.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.234
So I went to him the next day.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.467
"We're going to do a petition
called Wong for Wong."

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.801
[ Laughter ]
"You sign it.

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:20.467
Cumberbatch signs it.
That's it."

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:23.501
He's not having any of this.
-Of course, yeah, yeah.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.634
Wong for Wong, no.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.400
-Yeah, so then that's
out of the window.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.734
Cut to a few months later,
I'm filming in Budapest.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:34.234
I get this mysterious e-mail
with, "Hi, we would like you

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:36.167
to audition for
the part of Lee."

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:39.534
So I was like, "Alright, yes."
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:43.968
Went on tape, did some tweaks
in Slovakia.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.701
By the time I got to Malaysia,

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:48.234
I got the call from
the amazing Sarah Finn.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.834
"Congratulations, you're going
to have a wonderful time."

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.067
I text my friend Chiwetel.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.834
"I'm going to have to
borrow your lawyer."

00:02:55.834 --> 00:03:00.367
And he replied back,
"Wong for Wong?"

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.701
And I replied, "Wong is Wong."

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:06.234
-Yeah, that's right.
Wong is Wong.

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:08.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
You made it happen.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.167
You made it work.
-And I'm here.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.100
-And you're here
and you're great.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.267
-Thank you.
-When you were growing up,

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.667
you said you were
a big Spider-Man fan.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:19.801
-Yeah, massive.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:22.367
-You got to be in
"Spider-Man: No Way Home,"

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.300
one of the biggest movies ever.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.300
But a lot of people
don't know this.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.000
You actually played Spider-Man
once before yourself.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.200
You were Spider-Man.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.000
-Yeah, Spider-Wong.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.767
-Where can we see you
as Spider-Wong?

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:40.501
-Well, a long, long, long,
long time ago, Sia,

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:45.100
the amazing singer that is Sia
had called me up for her video

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.834
"Breathe Me,"

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:49.667
you know, and said like, "Come
on, I want you to be in this."

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.767
You know, I was trying to say,

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.267
"Look, I'm trying to be
a serious actor.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:56.667
I don't know if I should be
in music videos.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.434
What do you want me to do?"

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:01.434
"You can either wear a rabbit
costume or a Spider-Man outfit."

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.067
I went, "I'll be over
in 15 minutes."

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.868
So I got to my chance
to play Spider-Man.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:09.901
-This is kind of awesome
right here. Here's you.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:13.234
There's you as Spider-Man.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.667
This one -- I probably should've
showed this one.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.267
-Oh, yeah, there I am
in full costume.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.601
So there we go.
-Yeah, that's you right there.

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.334
Yes, you actually have played
Spider-Man before.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.667
-Yes, I have.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.534
-But now fans are freaking out
because they love you.

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:28.901
They want the MCU to be the WCU.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.634
They want
the Wong Cinematic Universe.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:38.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.634
Make sure you got
the U just right.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:43.467
But fans do want you to have
your own Disney+ series.

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:44.667
What do you think of that?

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.667
Do you have ideas
for story lines?

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.901
-For all of those feelings in
the 312 Wong-tourage fans.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.200
-Wong-tourage?

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.100
-Yeah, that's what
I affectionately call them now.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.667
-The Wong-tourage. I love that.
That's going to catch on.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.634
-We have to give them
what they want, clearly.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:03.000
-There's 312 people
demanding this.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.734
-Don't you think?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.300
I can't hear you!

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.400
[ Cheers and applause
intensify ]

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.133
-Wow!
-Oh, wow.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.968
-People are demanding it.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.167
-Showing you some of
my pantomime skills there.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.968
-Yeah, you're actually very
talented, yeah.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.868
But I think that would be great.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.767
I mean, would you be up
for that?

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:23.400
-I'd love it. I'd love it.
-You would?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.434
Yeah, they do good work
over at Disney+.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:28.234
There's got to be backstories
and stuff that we don't know.

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:31.000
-Yeah, you know, what happens to
Wong during the infinity war.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.467
You know, there's a five-year
period we can start with.

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.634
-What do you think happened?

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.033
-Well, he took a deep breath

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.067
'cause it was really full-on
out there, wasn't it?

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.901
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.467
-He could've done anything.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.534
You know, training his students
at Kamar-Taj maybe.

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:48.868
-Oh, yeah.
I'd love to know that --

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:50.400
what happens at Kamar-Taj,
what happens at --

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.200
Yeah, a day in the life.
-Yeah.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.567
-I would love to see.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.300
Yeah, maybe there can be
a scientist.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.334
-You should be in it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:00.534
-That's your idea.
I mean, if the people want it.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:03.601
-I think Jimmy should be in it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.734
Come on, Jimmy,
give me some action.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.200
Give me some portals.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.200
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.534
-Yeah, right? You feel that?

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.267
-Health and Safety
will patch that up.

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.467
-Let's talk "Doctor Strange."

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:18.601
This is a giant,
giant, giant movie.

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:19.734
Congrats.
-Thank you.

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:21.734
-And I would recommend seeing it
in IMAX too

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:25.000
if you can do it because it is
a big, big universe.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.234
Multiverse, really.
And it really is. It pays off.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:31.934
There's probably -- yeah,
100 different places you go to.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.634
-Yeah.
-It's just a giant world.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:35.567
I don't know.
It's so amazing to me.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.801
I go, "What's real and how do
you act in this?"

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:42.100
-Well, Charles Wood is amazing
at building the set design.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.767
And obviously we have
the green screen

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:46.968
that takes us to
far-reaching places.

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:50.467
But, you know, massive credit to
the VFX team.

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:52.200
-They do a great job.
What can we say?

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.033
What happens in this movie?

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:55.701
-A lot happens.

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:59.467
I mean, from those that have
seen "Wandavision"

00:06:59.467 --> 00:07:03.167
and "No Way Home," obviously
the spell that I told him

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.501
not to cast has been cast.

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:08.133
The cracks in the parallel
realities are open.

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:09.934
All sorts of characters
are coming out,

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:12.501
and all roads lead to our movie.

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:14.467
-Yeah, congratulations.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.734
Here's Benedict Wong in

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:18.200
"Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness."

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.367
Take a look at this.

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:21.767
-Spider-Man -- he has the powers
of a spider.

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:23.801
-Hence the name.
-Gross.

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.000
Does he look like a spider?
-No, no, more like a man.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.868
-Climbs walls. Shoots webs.
-Yeah, bingo.

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:29.234
-Out of his butt?
-No.

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:31.334
-Ew.
-Maybe, I don't know.

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:35.701
Honestly, I hope not.
-Super weird.

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.167
-You're going to get
a stomach ache.

00:07:37.167 --> 00:07:38.701
-I'm from another universe.

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.667
How do you know my stomach works
the same as yours?

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:42.367
-I don't.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.667
I don't even know if you're
from another universe,

00:07:44.667 --> 00:07:45.968
which is why I'm still
sitting here

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:47.667
waiting for you to enlighten us.

00:07:52.634 --> 00:07:54.334
-[ Chuckles ]
-Which means...?

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:03.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Benedict Wong, everybody.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:05.667
"Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness"

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:07.968
is in theaters and IMAX
tomorrow.

